ore of a lead, eventually winning by almost four seconds over Canada, setting a world record of 3:39.30 in the process. Australia won bronze, with West Germany trailing in fourth. As the pro-USA audience cheered their boys wildly, on the side of the pool, American breaststroker " [:a {:href "/athletes/51470"} "Steve Lundquist"] " unfurled a towel, on which he had printed, “America … than you for a dream come true!”"] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "3:44.33 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "3:39.30 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Backstroke"] [:td {:class "bib"} "454"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51287"} "Rick Carey"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Breaststroke"] [:td {:class "bib"} "472"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51470"} "Steve Lundquist"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Butterfly"] [:td {:class "bib"} "476"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51497"} "Pablo Morales"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Freestyle"] [:td {:class "bib"} "461"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51352"} "Rowdy Gaines"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Backstroke"] [:td {:class "bib"} "490"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51617"} "Dave Wilson"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [: